 ## Roles in schools that already exist
 Permission `sessions.view` for student, guardian, principal, branch principal, teacher and bursar. Roles in existing environments are brought up to date in two steps on every deploy: `npm run sync:registries` (updates the platform's role templates: locked ones are made exact, editable ones only gain missing permissions) and then `npm run sync:school-roles` (updates each school's own copy; roles a school has customised are skipped and listed). See `ROLE_SYNC_NOTES.md`. Until both have run, the affected roles get `PERMISSION_DENIED` on `/sessions/current`.
 
+## Unique names are database rules (migration `20261027100000_unique_names`)
+Session name (ignoring capitals and spaces at the ends) and one term of each name per session are now enforced by the database, so two requests at the same moment cannot both succeed. The app check stays (it gives the friendly error first); when a race gets past it, the database refuses the second and the API answers the same `SESSION_NAME_TAKEN` / `TERM_NAME_TAKEN` as before. The indexes exist only in the SQL (Prisma cannot declare the case-insensitive one); `Term_sessionId_name_key` is the same rule Prisma would name.
+Existing data: later duplicate sessions are renamed `<name> (duplicate 2)`, `(duplicate 3)`... (the oldest keeps its name). Duplicate terms in one session cannot be renamed or merged safely, so the migration stops with a message naming the session and term: fix by hand, then run it again. Date-overlap rules stay app-only (admin-only, rare).
+
 ## Frontend changes
 - `GET /sessions/current` returns `{ session, currentTerm }` (before: the session).
 - Terms carry `session: { id, name }` instead of `sessionId` (terms listed inside a session omit it). Calendar events carry `term: { id, name }` and `session: { id, name }` instead of `termId` and `sessionId`.
diff --git a/prisma/tenant-migrations/20261027100000_unique_names/migration.sql b/prisma/tenant-migrations/20261027100000_unique_names/migration.sql
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3f434f2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/prisma/tenant-migrations/20261027100000_unique_names/migration.sql
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+-- Names that must be unique, enforced by the database itself (so two requests at the same moment cannot both
+-- succeed). The app already refuses these names; this closes the race. Prisma cannot declare the case-insensitive
+-- indexes in the schema file, so they live only here.
+--   Session  : name, ignoring capitals and spaces at the ends
+--   Term     : one of each term per session
+--   Class    : name, ignoring capitals and spaces at the ends
+--   Subject  : name, ignoring capitals and spaces at the ends (code was already unique)
+
+-- Existing data first. Sessions, classes and subjects: the OLDEST keeps its name; each later duplicate is renamed
+-- "<name> (duplicate 2)", "(duplicate 3)" ... so no record is lost and a school can tidy them afterwards.
+-- Terms cannot be renamed (the name is one of First/Second/Third) and grades, attendance and invoices hang off
+-- them, so nothing is merged or guessed: the migration stops with a clear message instead.
+DO $$
+DECLARE
+    t RECORD;
+BEGIN
+    SELECT s."name" AS session_name, tm."name"::text AS term_name INTO t
+    FROM "Term" tm JOIN "Session" s ON s."id" = tm."sessionId"
+    GROUP BY s."name", tm."sessionId", tm."name" HAVING count(*) > 1 LIMIT 1;
+    IF FOUND THEN
+        RAISE EXCEPTION 'Session "%" has the term "%" more than once. Fix this by hand (move or remove the extra term), then run the migration again.', t.session_name, t.term_name;
+    END IF;
+END $$;
+
+UPDATE "Session" x SET "name" = btrim(x."name") || ' (duplicate ' || d.rn || ')'
+FROM (SELECT "id", row_number() OVER (PARTITION BY lower(btrim("name")) ORDER BY "createdAt", "id") AS rn FROM "Session") d
+WHERE x."id" = d."id" AND d.rn > 1;
+
+UPDATE "Class" x SET "name" = btrim(x."name") || ' (duplicate ' || d.rn || ')'
+FROM (SELECT "id", row_number() OVER (PARTITION BY lower(btrim("name")) ORDER BY "createdAt", "id") AS rn FROM "Class") d
+WHERE x."id" = d."id" AND d.rn > 1;
+
+UPDATE "Subject" x SET "name" = btrim(x."name") || ' (duplicate ' || d.rn || ')'
+FROM (SELECT "id", row_number() OVER (PARTITION BY lower(btrim("name")) ORDER BY "createdAt", "id") AS rn FROM "Subject") d
+WHERE x."id" = d."id" AND d.rn > 1;
+
+-- CreateIndex
+CREATE UNIQUE INDEX "Session_name_lower_key" ON "Session"(lower(btrim("name")));
+CREATE UNIQUE INDEX "Term_sessionId_name_key" ON "Term"("sessionId", "name");
+CREATE UNIQUE INDEX "Class_name_lower_key"   ON "Class"(lower(btrim("name")));
+CREATE UNIQUE INDEX "Subject_name_lower_key" ON "Subject"(lower(btrim("name")));
